      {
        "id": "what-is-engine-knock-and-why-is-it-critical",
        "title": "What is engine knock — and why is it critical?",
        "description": null,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "cards",
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "What is engine knock?",
                "text": "📖",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "📖",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "📖 What is engine knock? Engine knock (also known as detonation) is the abnormal combustion of air-fuel mixture in the cylinders, causing a metallic knocking sound and potentially serious engine damage."
              },
              {
                "title": "Why it matters",
                "text": "⚠️",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "⚠️",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "⚠️ Why it matters If left unresolved, engine knock can lead to piston, bearing and cylinder damage, resulting in extremely high repair costs or even complete engine failure."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "⚙️"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "KEY TAKEAWAY"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Engine knock is a warning sign. The sooner you identify and resolve the cause, the more likely you can avoid major engine damage and costly repairs."
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "what-is-engine-knock-and-why-is-it-critical",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
